SUMMARY:Ali Wong Live at Neal S Blaisdell Concert Hall (Saturday)
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. \nAbout the Performer\nAli Wong is one of the most celebrated stand-up comedians of her generation. Known for her fearless\, raw\, and unapologetically honest humor\, she burst into mainstream consciousness with her Netflix specials Baby Cobra (2016) and Hard Knock Wife (2018)\, both filmed while she was visibly pregnant — a bold comedic choice that became her signature. \nHer comedy dives deep into marriage\, motherhood\, sex\, and the immigrant experience with a sharp wit and zero filter. She has since starred in the Netflix romantic comedy film Always Be My Maybe (2019)\, which she co-wrote\, and the critically acclaimed Hulu series Beef (2023)\, for which she won an Emmy Award. Ali Wong is a true force in comedy — and her live shows are legendary for their energy and intimacy. \nThis Saturday show was added after the Friday July 24 show sold out almost immediately — a testament to Ali Wong’s massive popularity in Hawaii and her deep connection to the islands. \nEvent Details\n\nDate: Saturday\, July 25\, 2026\nTime: 7:00 PM HST (Doors open earlier)\nVenue: Neal S Blaisdell Concert Hall\, 777 Ward Avenue\, Honolulu\, HI 96814\nShow Duration: Approximately 90 minutes\nAge Restrictions: All ages welcome\n\nAbout the Venue\nThe Neal S Blaisdell Concert Hall is Honolulu’s premier performing arts venue\, located at 777 Ward Avenue in the heart of the city. Part of the iconic Blaisdell Center complex\, the Concert Hall seats approximately 2\,158 guests and is renowned for its excellent acoustics and intimate atmosphere despite its size. \nThe venue features comfortable theater-style seating\, multiple concession areas\, and easy access to parking in the adjacent Blaisdell Center parking structure. Valet parking is also available for added convenience. The surrounding area offers a variety of dining and entertainment options\, making it easy to turn the evening into a full night out in Honolulu. \nThe Blaisdell Concert Hall has hosted some of the world’s biggest names in entertainment\, from classical orchestras to top-tier comedians. Its central location makes it easily accessible from Waikiki and downtown Honolulu. \nWhat to Expect\nAli Wong’s live show is a solo stand-up performance — no opening acts\, just Ali on stage delivering her signature brand of comedy for approximately 90 minutes. Expect a high-energy\, laugh-out-loud evening filled with stories about her life\, relationships\, and observations on modern culture. \nThis is the second and final Honolulu show — added specifically because the Friday show sold out so fast. If you missed out on Friday tickets\, this is your chance. Arrive early to find your seats and enjoy the venue’s amenities before the show begins. \nAli Wong’s Honolulu performances are always special events. Her connection to Hawaii and her fans here makes for an unforgettable night of comedy. \nTicket Information\nPrice Range: $100 – $127+ (resale prices may vary) \nPurchase official tickets directly through Ticketmaster\, or find resale tickets through VividSeats for flexible options including pairs and premium seating. \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
